## 33. REQUIRED POWER-UP BEHAVIOR

### SHUNT

Forward homing projectile.

Backward non-homing projectile.

Must be:

- Visible.
- Avoidable.
- Interceptable.
- Physically impactful.
- Clearly announced to the targeted player.

### BOLT

One pickup provides three individual shots.

Each shot:

- Travels independently.
- Has projectile collision.
- Can fire forward or backward.
- Updates ammunition.

### BARGE

Radial shockwave around the vehicle.

Must physically push nearby opponents and destroy supported incoming projectiles and nearby mines.

### MINE

Deploy behind or throw forward.

Must be visible, avoidable, destructible where configured and physically relevant.

### SHOCK

Create three avoidable electrical hazards ahead of the race leader.

Placement must use actual distance-based track progress.

### SHIELD

Actual defensive energy barrier.

Protects according to explicit combat rules.

Has duration and absorption capacity.

### NITRO

Collected inventory item.

Forward activation produces temporary acceleration.

Backward activation performs the airbrake maneuver followed by boost.

### REPAIR

Restore missing segmented health.

Initial proposed repair capacity: four health blocks.

Never exceed vehicle maximum durability.

Update visible damage.

